console.log(typeof myInstance); // "object"

console.log(myInstance instanceof MyClass); // true
```

In this example, `typeof myInstance` returns `"object"` because `myInstance` is an instance of the `MyClass` class. However, `myInstance instanceof MyClass` returns `true` because `myInstance` is indeed an instance of the `MyClass` class.

