namespace App\Http\Middleware;

use Closure;
use Illuminate\Support\Facades\Auth;

class BlockIpMiddleware
{
    /**
     * Handle an incoming request.
     *
     * @param  \Illuminate\Http\Request  $request
     * @param  \Closure  $next
     * @return mixed
     */
    public function handle($request, Closure $next)
    {
        // Define the allowed IP addresses
        $allowedIps = ['192.168.0.1', '192.168.0.2'];

        // Get the user's IP address
        $ipAddress = $request->ip();

        // Check if the user's IP address is in the allowed list
        if (!in_array($ipAddress, $allowedIps)) {
            return response()->json(['error' => 'Access denied'], 403);
        }

        return $next($request);
    }
}
```

In this example, we define an array `$allowedIps` containing the IP addresses that are allowed access. We then retrieve the user's IP address from the request and check if it is in the allowed list. If the IP address is not allowed, we return a JSON response with an error message and a status code of 403 (Forbidden).

